Verified every Codex finding against `spec/v0.4/README.md`, `event.schema.json`, `DECISIONS.md`, and
external sources (RFC 9073 checked directly at rfc-editor.org: `PARTICIPANT` component + `PARTICIPANT-TYPE`
with registered value `SPEAKER`, Standards Track, *Updates: 5545* — confirmed). Outcome: **broad
agreement, no genuine dispute.** All findings accepted. Changes made to `proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md`
and `proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json`:

### P035 — accepted all three; verdict stays "into v0.5 with changes"

- **MAJOR (iCal RFC 9073):** accepted. iCal mapping row rewritten — "RFC 5545 core has no speaker term;
  enhanced iCalendar (RFC 9073) MAY emit `PARTICIPANT` with `PARTICIPANT-TYPE:SPEAKER`, `CN`←`name`,
  `URL`←`url`; else `X-OTE-SPEAKER` / `DESCRIPTION`. `ATTENDEE` stays forbidden."
- **MINOR (schema.org `url` not `sameAs`):** accepted. Mapping now: `url`→`url` normative, `sameAs` only as
  an exporter MAY when it knows the URL is an identity profile.
- **MINOR (list order):** accepted. `$defs/speakers` description now states "a list in DISPLAY / preference
  order — the first survives to single-value destinations", matching `organizers`/`image`, plus "only
