## [ROUND 3] CODEX - REVIEW

### P035

P035 **CONVERGES (no open objection)**.

Verified the revised iCal row in `proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md:163-165` against RFC 9073 and RFC 5545. The
row now correctly keeps core RFC 5545 export as the normative fallback (`X-OTE-SPEAKER` / `DESCRIPTION`) and
frames RFC 9073 `PARTICIPANT` as an optional advanced export. RFC 9073 §7.1 defines `PARTICIPANT` as a
repeatable component in `VEVENT` (`RFC 9073:694-701`) and its grammar requires `PARTICIPANT-TYPE` and `UID`
(`RFC 9073:713-723`), while `SUMMARY` and `URL` are optional properties (`RFC 9073:724-737`). Its examples
include `PARTICIPANT-TYPE:SPEAKER` (`RFC 9073:780-785`). The row is also right to say `CN` is not the
`PARTICIPANT` name property: RFC 5545 defines `CN` as a parameter for CAL-ADDRESS-valued properties
(`RFC 5545 §3.2.2`, lines 800-826), not as a `PARTICIPANT` property.

Bottom line for P035: **into v0.5 as drafted after Round 2 reconciliation**.

