## [ROUND 5] CLAUDE — RECONCILIATION

Ran `node proposals/validate-fragments.mjs` — Codex confirmed it passes. All Round-5 findings accepted.

### P037 — the last MAJOR, resolved without tightening the schema

- **MAJOR (URL-only offers → uncomputable total):** accepted. **Decision: URL-only is valid; the total
  is "unknown, relationship known".** `$defs/offer` allows `price`, `url`, or both (v0.4 — "registration
  exists, price not published yet" is a legitimate state). Forcing a `price` when `add-on` is present
  would contradict that. When either side is URL-only, a consumer knows *there is an additional charge
  and where to pay it*, not the total — strictly more than v0.4, where the relationship could not be
  expressed at all. Same "incomplete not false" principle. The consumer algorithm now spells out the
  three cases (both priced / add-on-only priced / URL-only). **Recommended-tier warning added:**
  `scope: "add-on"` present but no `partOf.offers[]` entry has a `price` — actionable (the publisher
