## [ROUND 6] CODEX — REVIEW

Scope: P037 only. P035/P036/P038 were not re-reviewed.

### Validator Result

Ran `node proposals/validate-fragments.mjs` twice; both runs pass with `ALL 36 CASES CLASSIFIED AS EXPECTED`. The new URL-only cases are real event-schema cases: `proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:93-96` marks URL-only admission, URL-only add-on, and URL-only on both sides as valid. The four `sharedOffersConsistent` cases are feed-level probes over the reference implementation: identical offers with object-member order swapped passes, differing price fails, array order differs fails, and one sibling omitting `partOf.offers` passes as warning territory (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:145-158`).

### Item 1 — Round-5 MAJOR

Resolved. The proposal now explicitly defines URL-only offers as "relationship known / total unknown", not as computable totals. Evidence: the `scope` table says `add-on` is a priced admission plus add-on price only when both carry numbers, otherwise "there is an additional charge, total unknown" (`v0.5-event-fields.md:464-467`). The Round-5 clarification says `$defs/offer` may be price, URL, or both; if either side has no `price`, no number is emitted and no wrong number is emitted (`v0.5-event-fields.md:475-481`). The consumer algorithm gives non-numeric outputs for partial pricing: "admission + <entry.price> extra" or "admission + extra fee, see <entry.url>" (`v0.5-event-fields.md:517-534`). No consumer is forced to invent a number.

Recommendation: carry those three consumer-output cases into README examples during implementation; they are the important part of the semantics.

### Item 2 — Round-5 MINOR

Resolved for proposal review. The actual v0.5 implementation still needs a feed-root custom keyword, but the proposal now has a reviewable reference implementation and feed-level tests. Evidence: `deepEqualJson` and `sharedOffersConsistent` are in `proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:119-143`, and the four feed cases are in `proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:145-158`. The proposal says this remains a feed-root validator error via a custom keyword because only the feed root sees siblings (`v0.5-event-fields.md:579-584`).

Recommendation: when implementing `spec/v0.5/feed.schema.json`, add the real custom keyword and keep these four cases as invalid/valid examples or unit tests.

### deepEqualJson Fidelity Check

Faithful to the proposal definition. `deepEqualJson` treats null/undefined as absent (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:119-122`), compares numbers by JS numeric value so JSON `45` and `45.0` collapse the same way after parse (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:123`), compares strings/bools exactly without coercion (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:124`), keeps array order significant (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:125-126`), and sorts object keys while filtering null/undefined values so member order is insignificant (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:127-129`). That matches the proposal text, including translations-map member-order insensitivity and omitted siblings (`v0.5-event-fields.md:586-594`; fragment text at `v0.5-schema-fragments.json:70-73`).

Recommendation: preserve the "null treated as absent" rule as a comparison-only belt-and-braces rule; base schema still rejects typed nulls before this should matter.

### Recommended-Tier Warning Scoping Check

Correctly scoped. The warning "`scope: add-on` present but no `partOf.offers[]` entry carries a `price`" is per-event because `addOnRequiresSetAdmission` requires the relevant `partOf.offers` in the same document (`v0.5-schema-fragments.json:42-66`), and the proposal states no `partOf.id` resolution is used for pricing (`v0.5-event-fields.md:517-520`). No feed-root view is needed for that warning. The separate missing-set-price-across-siblings warning remains feed-root, as stated (`v0.5-event-fields.md:601-610`).

Recommendation: keep these as two distinct recommended checks: per-event unpriced base admission for add-ons, feed-root incomplete sibling coverage.

### Anything Else Open

No open P037 objection remains. The narrowed Model A is now explicit: one shared admission, any tier, plus flat add-ons; tier-specific coverage, per-day passes, bundles, group rates, coupons, and reverse bundles are out of scope with Model B documented as the next step (`v0.5-event-fields.md:537-555`). The DECISIONS.md plan covers the primary breaking decision and the required cross-references to D009/D010/D023/D011/D012/D021/D030, with D004/D015/D025 noted as no semantic change (`v0.5-event-fields.md:646-661`).

Bottom line: **P037 CONVERGES** into v0.5 as a deliberate `0.5.0` breaking change, with the listed implementation work: `partOf.offers`, `offers[].scope`, `addOnRequiresSetAdmission`, real feed-root `sharedOffersConsistent`, recommended pricing checks, translation rule-site updates, README/reference wording changes, migration/adopter scan, and a new primary DECISIONS.md entry. The whole P035-P038 proposal is now done.

