## [ROUND 7] CODEX — REVIEW

Scope: P039/P040 only. P035-P038 were not re-reviewed. `gh issue view 25/26 --repo openTechEvents/opentechevents-spec` failed with `error connecting to api.github.com`, so this review is grounded in the proposal, fragments, validator, and local spec/docs. Ran `node proposals/validate-fragments.mjs`: it passes with `ALL 49 CASES CLASSIFIED AS EXPECTED`; the validator compiles both injected event and feed schemas (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:45-61`) and exercises P039/P040 cases at `proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:184-198`.

### P039

- **MINOR — "Informational, no sync guarantee" is the right consumer contract, but the producer-side duty should be stated more sharply.** Evidence: the proposal correctly says the linked resources may drift and consumers must treat `alternates` as "another representation the publisher points to", not guaranteed same data (`v0.5-event-fields.md:802-809`). The existing Discovery section already frames `<link rel="alternate">` as a discovery mechanism, not a validation/sync mechanism (`spec/v0.4/README.md:852-860`). Recommendation: keep "informational" and add one producer sentence: alternates SHOULD be generated from the same source or otherwise intended to describe the same collection, but consumers MUST NOT assume exact sync, completeness, or derivation.

- **MINOR — The `mediaType` pattern is fine for common feed types, but the no-parameters/lowercase policy needs to be explicit.** Evidence: the fragment pattern is `^[a-z]+/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]*$` (`v0.5-schema-fragments.json:110-114`). It accepts `application/rss+xml`, `application/atom+xml`, `application/feed+json`, `application/ld+json`, `text/calendar`, and vendor-style `application/vnd.api+json`; it rejects `application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8` and uppercase `Application/RSS+XML` in my direct regex probe. That is defensible if this field stores a canonical media type token, not a full HTTP `Content-Type` header value. Recommendation: document "lowercase media type only, no parameters"; add validator cases for `application/atom+xml`, `application/feed+json`, and rejected `; charset=utf-8`.

- **NIT — Allowing repeated `mediaType` values and dropping `title` are acceptable, but only for mirror semantics.** Evidence: the proposal allows two entries with the same media type and says a consumer that can show one shows the first (`v0.5-event-fields.md:794-800`); the validator confirms same-media-type RSS mirrors are valid and exact duplicates reject (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:186-189`). Recommendation: add a sentence that same-`mediaType` entries SHOULD be mirrors or equivalent choices, not semantically different feeds that need a human label; if a real case needs labels, revisit `title` as already noted (`v0.5-event-fields.md:840-842`).

Bottom line: **into v0.5 with changes**: keep feed-only `alternates`, keep informational/no-sync semantics, keep same-media-type mirrors and no `title`, but clarify lowercase/no-parameter media types, add the three media-type validator cases, and add the producer SHOULD about same-source/same-collection intent. No D001-D031 decision is directly reopened; this updates Discovery prose and shares P037's generic 0.5.0 extension-collision migration scan.

### P040

- **MAJOR — The proposal says there is a shared `$defs.contributing`, but the fragment and validator inline the property instead.** Evidence: P040 prose says "`$defs` — a plain string, reused at both levels" (`v0.5-event-fields.md:885-893`) and the implementation checklist says "a shared string `$def`" (`v0.5-event-fields.md:987-990`). The fragment has only `feedAndEvent.properties.contributing` as an inline string property (`v0.5-schema-fragments.json:51-62`) and no `$defs.contributing`; the validator injects that inline property into the event schema and strips `x-inheritsFrom` for the feed copy (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:29-33`, `56-60`). Recommendation: add `$defs.contributing` and have both feed/event properties `$ref` it; put `x-inheritsFrom: "feed.contributing"` only as a sibling annotation on the event property.

- **NIT — Keep the name `contributing`, not `contributingUrl` or `correctionsUrl`.** Evidence: the value is broader than error reports: the real producer is the OTE editor, whose tool entry says `?repo=owner/name` reads a preset and proposes changes via issue-to-PR (`docs/data/tools.json`, editor entry; proposal evidence at `v0.5-event-fields.md:863-869`). `correctionsUrl` is too narrow for "fix or contribute a data change"; `contributingUrl` is clearer mechanically but redundant if the schema type is always HTTP(S), and `licenseUrl` is only split because `license` itself is SPDX-or-URL (`v0.5-event-fields.md:896-900`). Recommendation: keep `contributing`, but make the generated reference label unambiguous: "URL for reporting or proposing data changes."

- **NIT — Feed-to-event default inheritance is the right model, including event override.** Evidence: the feed section already has default inheritance for scalar `specVersion`, `license`, and `textLanguage`, while `translations` is explicitly not inherited (`spec/v0.4/README.md:788-803`; `spec/v0.4/reference.en.md:11`). The proposed `contributing` is a scalar correction channel, not translated content, so declared event value replacing feed value is the least surprising rule (`v0.5-event-fields.md:871-875`). The event-level copy is justified by aggregated events that should point at a community repo rather than the aggregator's generic channel (`v0.5-event-fields.md:931-933`). Recommendation: add `contributing` to the README inheritance table and generated reference defaults; no new keyword is needed.

- **NIT — The field does not materially overlap `source.url` or `organizers[].email`.** Evidence: `source` is provenance for imported/aggregated data (`spec/v0.4/event.schema.json:1009-1011`; `reference.en.md:85-88`), while organizers are who run the event and aggregators must omit feed-level organizers to avoid false attribution (`spec/v0.4/feed.schema.json:55-57`; `spec/v0.4/README.md:792`). P040's channel is for fixing this record, including aggregator mapping errors (`v0.5-event-fields.md:853-861`). Recommendation: keep all three separate and include one example with both `source.url` and `contributing` so consumers see the distinction.

Bottom line: **into v0.5 with changes**: add the missing shared `$defs.contributing` and `$ref` it from both feed/event copies; keep the field name `contributing`, feed-to-event scalar inheritance, event override, string-only shape, and not-recommended status. This touches the README inheritance table and reference generation, but does not reopen D001-D031; it cross-references the existing inheritance pattern from D016/D029 rather than changing it.

