## [ROUND 9] CODEX - REVIEW

Validator check: `node proposals/validate-fragments.mjs` still reports `ALL 62 CASES CLASSIFIED AS EXPECTED`.

### P035 / P038 speaker enrichment findings

- **MAJOR - Do not move `sameAs` into P035 core yet.** Evidence: P035 currently says `speakers[].url` is a single URL, "parallel to `organizers`" (`proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md`, P035 "`url` is a single URL"), and the schema fragment keeps `url` scalar under `$defs.speaker` (`proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json`, `$defs.speaker.properties.url`). schema.org does define `sameAs` on `Thing` as a URL that unambiguously indicates identity (https://schema.org/sameAs), so `Person.sameAs` is the right vocabulary for identity profiles; but Google Event structured-data docs list `performer` / `performer.name` examples and do not document nested `performer.sameAs` as an Event rich-result field (https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/event). Moving it into core now would add a second URL channel without a measured producer bar. **Recommendation:** keep P035 minimal and keep `sameAs` in P038; do not make `url` string-or-array.

- **MINOR - The Google claim for `sameAs` is too strong as drafted.** Evidence: the P035 "Deliberately NOT in the core" table says "`Google reads it for entity reconciliation`"; schema.org supports the property, but the Google Event documentation checked above does not list `sameAs` for nested performers. **Recommendation:** reword to "schema.org supports `Person.sameAs`; Google Event rich-result docs do not promise nested performer `sameAs` handling" unless a Google source is added.

- **MINOR - `affiliation` is acceptably translation-free, but the rule needs the proper-noun framing.** Evidence: schema.org `Person.affiliation` expects an `Organization` (https://schema.org/Person), and v0.4 already treats locality spellings as a single display choice rather than parallel translations (`spec/v0.4/README.md`, "What this version does not solve"). `Universitat de Valencia` / `University of Valencia` is closer to an organization display/legal name than free prose, but it has the same "choose the audience-recognizable spelling once" risk. **Recommendation:** keep `affiliation` out of translations, but say it is the organization display name written once, following the locality/organizer-name precedent.

- **MINOR - `speakers[].image` as an extension should warn about unpoliced nested translations.** Evidence: the P038 seed reuses `$defs/images`; v0.4/v0.5 translation machinery is defined for known schema sites, while P038 is explicitly non-normative and not part of validation (`proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json`, `suggestedExtensions.$comment`). **Recommendation:** add a P038 note that `speakers[].image[].translations` is only a suggested extension shape and will not receive core D010/D023/D030 validation until a future normative adoption.

- **MINOR - The registry shape should expose per-subfield status, not only `speakers.*`.** Evidence: P038 says the scan counts `speakers[].sameAs`, `speakers[].affiliation`, etc. separately, but the seed registry entry has one `"name": "speakers.*"` and one status. That is enough for prose, but weak for an adoption registry where `sameAs` may graduate while `bio` and `image` stay experimental. **Recommendation:** keep the umbrella page section, but model subfields as separate registry entries or a `subfields` map with independent counts/status.

- **NIT - Decisions touched: none if this stays non-normative.** Evidence: no P035 schema change is proposed, and P038 is described as a suggested-extension page. A future graduation of `sameAs` would need D026-style URL/userinfo treatment; `jobTitle`, `bio`, or `image` graduation would touch D010/D023/D030 translation validation. **Recommendation:** no DECISIONS.md change for Round 9; record those decision touchpoints only when a subfield graduates.

Bottom line: **right with changes** - keep P035 core minimal with single `url`; keep `sameAs`, `affiliation`, `jobTitle`, `bio`, and `image` in P038; qualify the Google `sameAs` claim; clarify `affiliation` as one display org name; warn that nested image translations in the extension are not core-validated; and make P038 adoption/status per-subfield.

