## [ROUND 10] CODEX - REVIEW

Validator check: `node proposals/validate-fragments.mjs` reports `ALL 67 CASES CLASSIFIED AS EXPECTED`. The new P035 cases exercise valid `sameAs`, empty list, exact duplicate, embedded userinfo, and non-HTTP rejection (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:90-94`).

### P035 `speakers[].sameAs`

- **MINOR - Core shape is coherent: keep `url` scalar and add `sameAs` array.** Evidence: the proposal keeps `url` as "one canonical URL" and `sameAs` as "the list of other profiles" (`proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md:181-197`); the schema matches that with scalar `url` and array `sameAs` (`proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json:165-184`). This is cleaner than `url` string-or-array because single-value destinations keep an unambiguous canonical page. **Recommendation:** keep `url` single; do not widen it to string-or-array.

- **MINOR - HTTP(S)-only `sameAs` is the right core rule, despite DID/AT/acct producer data.** Evidence: schema.org defines `sameAs` as the "URL of a reference Web page that unambiguously indicates the item's identity" and expects `URL` (https://schema.org/sameAs); `Person` inherits that property (https://schema.org/Person). The proposal's own bar says URL fields are HTTP(S) IRIs with no embedded userinfo (`proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md:87-90`), and the schema encodes `pattern: "^https?://"` (`proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json:179-182`). D020's domain-control argument is specific to `id`/`partOf.id` (`spec/v0.4/README.md:196`; `spec/v0.4/DECISIONS.md:405-421`), so it does not transfer wholesale; but the schema.org target does. A raw `did:plc:...`, `at://...`, or `acct:` value is an identifier/handle, not the Web page URL `sameAs` promises. **Recommendation:** reject non-HTTP schemes in core. Publishers with Bluesky/Fediverse data should emit the public HTTPS profile URL when available; raw decentralized identifiers can remain an extension until there is a separate identity-field proposal.

- **NIT - Softened Google wording is accurate.** Evidence: the P035 mapping now says Google does not document nested `performer.sameAs` (`proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md:254`). Google's Event structured-data docs list `performer` and `performer.name` only for that nested object; no `sameAs` entry is documented (https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/event). **Recommendation:** keep the softened wording; do not claim Google rich-result support for nested speaker profiles.

- **NIT - D026 userinfo extension is correctly applied.** Evidence: D026 rejects `@` in the HTTP(S) authority for public URL fields and explicitly covers both `user:pass@` and bare `user@` (`spec/v0.4/DECISIONS.md:523-533`). The new item schema uses the same `not: { "pattern": "^https?://[^/?#]*@" }` sibling as the existing URL fields (`proposals/v0.5-schema-fragments.json:179-182`), and the validator rejects `https://u:p@x.example` in `sameAs` (`proposals/validate-fragments.mjs:93`). **Recommendation:** no change.

- **NIT - One documentation caveat remains implicit but acceptable.** Evidence: `sameAs` is described as "Other profile pages for this SAME person" (`proposals/v0.5-event-fields.md:162-167`). That already rules out generic social search pages and non-profile homepages, but examples use only obvious profiles. **Recommendation:** optionally add one negative example later ("not a hashtag/search/team page"), but this is not required for v0.5.

Bottom line: **sameAs core shape is sound as drafted**. I would still have kept it in P038 on producer-bar grounds, but given hhkaos's inclusion decision, the field shape is the right one: `url` remains the canonical single HTTP(S) IRI; `sameAs` is an optional non-empty array of distinct HTTP(S) profile IRIs; raw DID/AT/acct identifiers stay out of core.

